  "question": {
    "text": "In an experiment with sonometer when a mass of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>180</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> is attached to the string, it vibrates with fundamental frequency of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Hz</mi></math>. When a mass&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math> is attached, the string vibrates with fundamental frequency of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>50</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Hz</mi></math>. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math> is ______ <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math>."
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "500",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>The formula to calculate the fundamental frequency in a stretched string is given by</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>L</mi></mrow></mfrac><msqrt><mfrac><mi>T</mi><mi>&#956;</mi></mfrac></msqrt><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>For the first mass, it can be written that</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>L</mi></mrow></mfrac><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mi>g</mi></mrow><mi>&#956;</mi></mfrac></msqrt><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>And, for the second mass, it can be written that</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>L</mi></mrow></mfrac><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>g</mi></mrow><mi>&#956;</mi></mfrac></msqrt><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>3</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>Divide equation (3) by equation (2) and simplify to obtain the required mass.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable columnalign=\"right center left\" columnspacing=\"0px\"><mtr><mtd><mfrac><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mfrac><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>L</mi></mrow></mfrac><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>g</mi></mrow><mi>&#956;</mi></mfrac></msqrt></mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>L</mi></mrow></mfrac><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mi>g</mi></mrow><mi>&#956;</mi></mfrac></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mo>&#160;</mo><msqrt><mfrac><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac></msqrt></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo>&#8658;</mo></mtd><mtd><mfrac><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mstyle></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msup><mfenced><mfrac><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo>&#8658;</mo></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mstyle></mfrac></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>4</mn></mfenced></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></p><p>Substitute the values of the known parameters into equation (4) to calculate the required mass.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable columnalign=\"right center left\" columnspacing=\"0px\"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mn>180</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mn>50</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Hz</mi></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mn>30</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Hz</mi></mstyle></mfrac></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>500</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></p></blockquote>"
  }
